  "solution": {
    "text": "The decreasing order of basicity is 3 &gt; 1 &gt; 2 &gt; 4.<br />The <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi></math> -carbon in <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/4875172d-bff5-422d-abf5-1d49a94facbe.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.16667in;height:0.50833in\" /> uses <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> -hybrid orbitals; while the <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi></math> -carbon in benzylamine uses <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> -hybrid orbitals. The electron-withdrawing <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> makes the phenyl ring even more electron-withdrawing and base-weakening.",
